WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.367
- All right, welcome back!

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.070
Even though Valentine's Day was Monday,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.320
you might still have a
few picked over chocolates

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.528
in that classic heart
shaped box lying around.

00:00:08.528 --> 00:00:10.576
Not in my house but some people might.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:14.480
If you do, our favorite Rustic
Joyful Food cookbook author

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.112
has a delicious way to
transform those leftover treats.

00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:19.253
Please welcome back, Danielle Kartes!

00:00:19.253 --> 00:00:20.520
(Kelly whooping)

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.370
- Yes, oh my gosh.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.213
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:22.213 --> 00:00:23.110
- This is awesome.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:23.943
I love my job.

00:00:23.943 --> 00:00:24.776
What are we making?

00:00:24.776 --> 00:00:27.500
- You guys, a lava cake is
like old school cruise ship

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.550
but it never goes outta style.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.420
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.610
- I love these things.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:31.910
Okay, so you know how
you were talkin' about

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.100
how you never have the chocolate left?

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.493
You know how you nibble on
one and it's kinda weird?

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:35.326
- Yeah.

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:36.159
And you're like, oh no.

00:00:36.159 --> 00:00:36.992
- Then you're like, oh
no, I don't like it.

00:00:36.992 --> 00:00:38.250
But then you're hard
up a couple days later

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.083
and you're like, I'm gonna eat that.

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:39.916
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:42.720
Okay, so this is a great way, these little

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.060
Valentine's cakes are a great way

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:44.934
to use up all the chocolate.
- Okay.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.790
- So first thing we're
gonna do, in your little

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.683
pretty bowl over there,
you've got eggs and sugar

00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:50.797
and chocolate already melted.

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:51.950
- I'm in.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:52.783
- [Danielle] You are in.

00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:54.380
And next thing we're
gonna do is add our flour.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.086
Sprinkle your flour across the whole top

00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:57.799
because you don't wanna over mix this.

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.355
We're not trying to overwork our flour.

00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:01.300
And when you overwork your flour,

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.210
that actually means you're
developing the gluten.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.050
You don't wanna do that.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.883
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.840
- Put your little vanilla in.
- Okay.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.673
- Put your salt in.

00:01:07.673 --> 00:01:08.760
Sprinkle 'em all over, all the salt.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.593
- Okay.
- We like it salty.

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:11.500
- I like it salty.
- And when you stir,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.330
take your spatula, this is
so cool, I don't know why.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.990
I always feel like cooking's
like therapy for me.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:16.823
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:17.656
- I just love it.

00:01:17.656 --> 00:01:18.489
- [Kelly] Especially baking.

00:01:18.489 --> 00:01:19.322
- Yes!

00:01:19.322 --> 00:01:20.155
- Okay, so go down the middle.

00:01:20.155 --> 00:01:21.219
Stir and fold.

00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:22.052
(Kelly gasps)

00:01:22.052 --> 00:01:23.547
Go all around the outside.
- What?

00:01:23.547 --> 00:01:25.700
- Down the middle, stir and fold.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.533
- How have I never learned this?

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:27.366
- Yes!

00:01:27.366 --> 00:01:28.592
This is makes you not have a tough cake.

00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:29.425
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:30.980
- You know when you're
baking your own cake,

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.110
I mean, shout out to box mix.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.050
I love a box mix.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:33.883
There's no shame in it.

00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:34.716
- Look, sometimes you don't have time.

00:01:34.716 --> 00:01:35.549
- You don't have time.

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:36.410
And we choose box mix.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.243
I mean, my kids choose it.

00:01:37.243 --> 00:01:38.076
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:39.272
- My vanilla cake is like, whatever.

00:01:39.272 --> 00:01:40.144
(audience laughs)

00:01:40.144 --> 00:01:43.280
So here, go in and you just barely wanna

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.740
get all the flour gone.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.634
- Okay.
- Keep on goin'.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.317
- [Kelly] You barely, so you
still wanna see a little?

00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:49.680
- You barely, you just wanna,
even if you see a couple bits

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.202
and little streaks of flour, it's fine.

00:01:51.202 --> 00:01:52.035
- Okay.

00:01:52.035 --> 00:01:52.868
I am done.
- So here we go.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.078
And then here's my other
little superhero tip.

00:01:55.078 --> 00:01:58.070
Your ice cream scoop wants more
action than just ice cream.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.370
- Aye!
- Isn't that cute?

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.330
